(
    title: "Cubicolor",
    developer: Some("Rob Fulop"),
    description: Some("Rob Fulop\'s take on Rubik\'s Race: slide the twenty-four coloured tiles of a five-by-five grid through its one empty space until the centre matches a generated three-by-three pattern, solo or racing a second player. Imagic wanted action games instead, so the finished puzzle never shipped — Fulop squirrelled away his fifty prototype carts and sold them to collectors years later, about sixty in all, making it a byword for 2600 rarity."),
